WEBVTT


00:00:15.647 --> 00:00:19.768
# It doesn't matter who you are #


00:00:19.836 --> 00:00:22.420
# I wish upon a shooting star #


00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:24.723
# That you will be the one #


00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.225
# Who comes to rescue me #


00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:31.007
"I love you"-- the most powerful
 phrase we utter as humans.


00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.698
We hear it
at every stage of life,


00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:36.301
and it always turns us
into kids again--


00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:40.538
wild, playful and with limited
control of our bodily functions.


00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:44.108
Love is a many splendored thing.
Love conquers all.


00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:47.178
Love is eternal until it ends.
- He'll love it.


00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:50.915
And that is where I come in.


00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:56.204
Being in love is the bestest, even
better than recess. I <i>love</i> love.


00:00:56.272 --> 00:01:00.041
My parents said they found love in the
back of a car and it helped create me.


00:01:04.313 --> 00:01:09.301
Hi, Tyler. You look, like,
hotter than Zach Morris today.


00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:12.136
I made you this.


00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:14.889
Wow, Britney. Thanks.


00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:20.111
I'm dumping you.
Heard you got cooties.


00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:25.433
Britney has cooties!


00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.337
Britney has cooties!
Britney has cooties!


00:01:29.372 --> 00:01:33.008
Nuh-uh. I was gonna dump him anyways.
Britney has cooties!


00:01:33.075 --> 00:01:36.994
Britney has cooties!
Britney has cooties!


00:01:37.062 --> 00:01:39.431
Britney has cooties!


00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:43.285
Um, sorry.
It's really catchy.


00:01:44.553 --> 00:01:46.654
Love blows!


00:01:56.081 --> 00:01:58.967
Love... blows.


00:02:00.769 --> 00:02:05.273
You're a great person, but this
relationship just isn't working out.


00:02:06.442 --> 00:02:09.677
It's time to move on...
for you,


00:02:09.745 --> 00:02:13.114
for me, for us.


00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:18.536
Sweetie, don't cry. This isn't good-bye.


00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:21.939
Okay? It's hello--
hello to a new friendship.


00:02:23.842 --> 00:02:26.311
Wait. Who are you again?


00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:29.538
I'm Britney. Your ex-boyfriend,
Sean, hired me to dump you.


00:02:29.539 --> 00:02:30.381
Oh, no.


00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:34.018
It's nothing personal.
It's-- It's what I do.


00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:36.187
I'm Britney Brooks,
the break-up artist.


00:02:37.589 --> 00:02:40.591
But seriously, I mean, you
met him on a reality TV show.


00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:42.660
You were doomed from day one.


00:02:48.584 --> 00:02:50.652
So how'd it go?


00:02:50.719 --> 00:02:54.539
She was a stage-three crier, Robyn. I
think I got tear stains on my Manolos.


00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:58.426
Ohh. Okay, your next client's
name is Linda.


00:02:58.494 --> 00:03:00.160
She needs to break
up with her boyfriend.


00:03:00.161 --> 00:03:02.580
She can't <i>stand</i> <i>being
in the same room with him.</i>


00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:06.918
Gary's just--
He's full of hot air.


00:03:06.985 --> 00:03:09.587
He's a liar, huh?


00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:13.174
No, no. He farts a lot,
and it's nasty.


00:03:13.241 --> 00:03:14.943
Oh.


00:03:15.011 --> 00:03:20.181
Wow. I mean, that was just
so clear and concise.


00:03:20.249 --> 00:03:22.384
Even I want to break up
with me now.


00:03:22.451 --> 00:03:25.353
Here. Um--


00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.573
On the back
is Dr. Stein's number.


00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:32.109
He's a gastroenterologist.


00:03:32.177 --> 00:03:36.080
Why would I need a stomach doctor?


00:03:39.301 --> 00:03:41.853
With your mother?


00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:47.255
We're gonna need something
with sprinkles, stat.


00:03:47.256 --> 00:03:47.626
Okay.


00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:50.962
Look, Marissa,
I know that it hurts,


00:03:51.029 --> 00:03:53.431
but that's what
I'm here for, okay?


00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.733
Men think all their past
discrepancies will be forgiven...


00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.135
with fresh roses
or chocolate nougats.


00:03:58.203 --> 00:04:02.273
I like nougat.
- No! That's your emotion talking.


00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:04.558
All right.
- Here's what you need to do.


00:04:04.626 --> 00:04:08.079
First, you need to get through the five
emotional stages of post breakup-dom.


00:04:08.146 --> 00:04:09.349
Stage one is denial.


00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:11.816
He can't break up
with me because I rock.


00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:12.706
Then anger.


00:04:12.707 --> 00:04:15.770
That fool, how dare
he deny my rockiness.


00:04:15.837 --> 00:04:18.172
Next is bargaining.


00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:22.310
Well, you know, maybe if I
did more when we have sex,


00:04:22.377 --> 00:04:24.478
he'd realize I rock.


00:04:24.546 --> 00:04:26.313
Then depression.


00:04:26.381 --> 00:04:29.583
Maybe I don't rock.


00:04:29.651 --> 00:04:31.669
And finally, acceptance.


00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:35.440
Screw him. I do rock.


00:04:36.992 --> 00:04:42.330
Wow. I've never seen someone go
through all the five stages so quickly.


00:04:42.398 --> 00:04:44.766
Honey, you're gonna
be fine.


00:04:47.202 --> 00:04:49.169
With my mother!


00:04:57.696 --> 00:05:00.047
Splitzville, Incorporated.


00:05:00.115 --> 00:05:02.116
When you're done kissing him,
we'll start dissing him.


00:05:02.184 --> 00:05:06.954
This is Tiffany.
How can I help? Yes.


00:05:07.022 --> 00:05:11.959
And we're also running a weekly special on
our "It's not you, it's me" break-up motif.


00:05:12.027 --> 00:05:15.880
Never ever wear silk to a break-up meeting,
especially when frosting is involved.


00:05:15.947 --> 00:05:18.215
Clients looking to end it all
are unpredictable.


00:05:18.283 --> 00:05:21.018
I mean, they're actually
thinking with their heart.


00:05:21.086 --> 00:05:22.971
What's wrong with that?


00:05:23.038 --> 00:05:26.240
The heart is a "special ed"
organ. It's not supposed to think.


00:05:26.308 --> 00:05:29.810
And when you use something for the
wrong purpose, it usually breaks.


00:05:29.878 --> 00:05:33.631
Ooh! Air kisses.
- Ashes.


00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:36.984
Come on, Brit.
Ashley is your sister.


00:05:37.052 --> 00:05:40.739
By blood only.
She's a spoiled, shallow brat...


00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:43.591
with the metabolism
of a frickin' Russian gymnast.


00:05:43.659 --> 00:05:47.328
I mean, her MySpace occupation
is "professional hottie."


00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.451
Oh.


00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:57.122
Oh, hey, Brit. We're going
clubbing tonight.


00:05:57.189 --> 00:06:01.175
If you stop giving off that
Ellen vibe, you can come.


00:06:01.243 --> 00:06:03.394
Why bother?


00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:06.214
Ninety-nine percent of all relationships
end with someone being dumped.


00:06:06.282 --> 00:06:09.967
And of the one percent who actually
get married, 50% end up divorced.


00:06:10.035 --> 00:06:13.137
You have a half a hundredth percent
chance of being in a loving relationship.


00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:19.410
Oh. Forgot. This is my boyfriend, Mike.
- Hi.


00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.546
Ash's new B.F., huh?


00:06:22.614 --> 00:06:27.051
Let me guess-- a plastic surgeon,
lawyer, movie producer?


00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:30.872
No, I teach art to disadvantaged
kids at the Y.M.C.A.


00:06:30.939 --> 00:06:33.658
<i>Actually, you know what? I just
entered my kids in a mural contest.</i>


00:06:33.725 --> 00:06:36.844
The winner gets 250 grand,
which would fund us for a year.


00:06:36.912 --> 00:06:40.581
So, if you guys ever have any
interest in coming to help us paint--


00:06:42.401 --> 00:06:45.553
Mm-mmm.
- She's so cute, isn't she?


00:06:45.621 --> 00:06:47.421
Are you gonna come
club with us, Mike?


00:06:47.489 --> 00:06:49.423
No, I'm just here
to drop Ashley off.


00:06:49.491 --> 00:06:51.526
I'm not actually
allowed to dance...


00:06:51.593 --> 00:06:54.762
because of a medical condition
known as being Caucasian.


00:06:56.581 --> 00:06:58.415
I've gotta go, sweetheart.


00:07:00.418 --> 00:07:04.922
I miss you already.
Um, bye.


00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:07.841
Really nice to meet
you guys. See ya.


00:07:07.909 --> 00:07:11.262
Wow, Ash, not bad. This one
actually casts a shadow.


00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.332
You'll be sick of him
by Friday.


00:07:14.399 --> 00:07:18.336
You're just jealous 'cause a man in
my life doesn't require batteries.


00:07:18.403 --> 00:07:21.639
Just once. Come out with us.


00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:26.693
I ended a lot of relationships today.


00:07:29.265 --> 00:07:30.898
Fine.


00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:45.062
Uh, you're giving off the "I'm
not into dudes" vibe again, honey.


00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:49.951
No, it's the "I just paid 11
bucks for a vodka cranberry" vibe.


00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:56.707
Brit, these guys are from that new
MTV show I was telling you about.


00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:59.710
They're rich and available.


00:07:59.778 --> 00:08:04.666
Before you begin, you should know that I don't
find either of you the least bit attractive.


00:08:07.368 --> 00:08:10.071
Oh. Okay, that was rude.


00:08:10.138 --> 00:08:15.309
No, that was honest. Rude is trying to set
someone up who doesn't want to be set up.


00:08:15.376 --> 00:08:19.097
Come on. Come, come.


00:08:28.389 --> 00:08:32.526
Um, these guys aren't
drunk enough to hit on Brit.


00:08:33.996 --> 00:08:36.363
Let's scare her up
a man.


00:08:40.902 --> 00:08:44.121
Chick dancing, guys? No.
I'm not--


00:08:47.025 --> 00:08:49.443
Hey, you're hot.


00:08:50.528 --> 00:08:53.397
Have I seen you
someplace before?


00:08:53.465 --> 00:08:57.234
Yeah. Yeah, you have.


00:08:57.302 --> 00:08:59.804
- That's why I don't go there anymore.
- Yeah, totally!


00:08:59.871 --> 00:09:02.006
Yeah.


00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:04.992
Hey, where are you going?
Don't be so picky.


00:09:07.046 --> 00:09:11.549
Stupid guys.
Stupid $11 drinks.


00:09:13.619 --> 00:09:15.853
Hi. I'm looking
for Britney Brooks.


00:09:15.921 --> 00:09:20.207
Look, the rumors are false. I'm not
looking for The L Word type action.


00:09:20.275 --> 00:09:24.928
I'm so sorry it's late.
It's just-- It's my boyfriend. I--


00:09:24.996 --> 00:09:27.632
It's okay. Come on in.


00:09:27.699 --> 00:09:31.185
I'm a convenience store--
always open.


00:09:31.253 --> 00:09:33.320
Rick is just
the most amazing guy.


00:09:33.388 --> 00:09:36.507
I mean, he's so kind
and caring and sensitive.


00:09:36.574 --> 00:09:41.612
<i>And his body,</i>
<i>it's just sick!</i>


00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.998
I mean, he does yoga.


00:09:44.066 --> 00:09:48.486
His Downward Dog, it's just--
it's just legendary.


00:09:48.553 --> 00:09:53.024
I mean, I'm treating him like
dirt right now, like icky dirt,


00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:57.561
not like that fancy, nutrient-rich
dirt that they sell at Home Depot.


00:10:02.551 --> 00:10:05.753
Can't I just break up
with him in person?


00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:09.389
It's a bad idea. Look, men
are genetically programmed...


00:10:09.457 --> 00:10:13.728
with an ability to convince us that they can
change when we're just about to dump them,


00:10:13.795 --> 00:10:18.248
that the second chance will be different
than the 12 others we've given them.


00:10:18.316 --> 00:10:21.168
Listen. As an independent
third party,


00:10:21.236 --> 00:10:26.490
I will be completely immune to all
his charms, pleas and pathetic cries.


00:10:26.558 --> 00:10:28.525
I'm the break-up artist.
It's what I do.


00:10:30.195 --> 00:10:32.196
Thank you.


00:10:39.171 --> 00:10:41.438
How do you handle this business?


00:10:41.506 --> 00:10:45.642
I mean, it's gotta be so depressing
dealing with everyone else's misery all day.


00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:50.647
Strong humans like me have a duty to
help people who actually believe in love,


00:10:50.716 --> 00:10:54.585
the ones who make tissue
and Prozac a necessity.


00:10:59.324 --> 00:11:01.558
Plus, I never take
my work home with me.


00:11:29.304 --> 00:11:32.839
You couldn't be anything else?
- Oh, you'll see.


00:11:32.907 --> 00:11:34.558
<i>I'll be back before you know it.</i>
<i>- I hope so.</i>


00:11:34.626 --> 00:11:38.679
Oh, my love, I shall miss you
every moment when you're gone.


00:11:40.415 --> 00:11:42.483
I love you, sweetheart.


00:11:42.551 --> 00:11:45.453
Hey, come on.
All aboard if you wanna get there.


00:11:51.559 --> 00:11:54.528
Thank God you're here.


00:11:54.595 --> 00:11:56.713
We thought you left with
one of those creepy club guys.


00:11:56.781 --> 00:11:59.583
I even watched the news this morning
to see if they found your dead body.


00:11:59.651 --> 00:12:04.554
<i>Your 1:00 just canceled. They said
they found another break-up service.</i>


00:12:04.622 --> 00:12:08.225
Probably another freelance dumper.
They never last.


00:12:08.293 --> 00:12:11.261
You don't mess with the best,
and that's Britney Brooks.


00:12:12.464 --> 00:12:16.300
She always talks about herself
in the third person.


00:12:16.367 --> 00:12:18.302
Tiffany hates that.


00:12:44.379 --> 00:12:46.981
Uh, excuse me.
I'm waiting for someone.


00:12:47.048 --> 00:12:49.750
Rick, right? Britney.


00:12:49.818 --> 00:12:52.652
Look, uh, Sally,


00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:56.039
she thinks you're a great
guy and she loves you,


00:12:56.107 --> 00:13:00.010
but, well, she's just
not in love with you.


00:13:00.078 --> 00:13:03.647
So, that's why she's
breaking up with you.


00:13:03.715 --> 00:13:06.833
Uh--
- It's not you. It's her.


00:13:09.337 --> 00:13:12.339
No, it's-- it's me.


00:13:14.193 --> 00:13:18.011
I should have treated
her better.


00:13:18.079 --> 00:13:21.382
The truth is, I never really felt
that spark with her, you know.


00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:24.434
I guess that's why I've been spending
so much time focusing on work recently.


00:13:24.502 --> 00:13:27.071
I run this dating
Web site called E-Mate.


00:13:27.139 --> 00:13:31.792
E-Mate. Yeah, I know you guys.
You keep me in business.


00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:36.013
Sally really is amazing.


00:13:36.081 --> 00:13:38.082
It's probably why
I couldn't let her go...


00:13:38.149 --> 00:13:40.017
even though I knew
she wasn't the one for me.


00:13:40.085 --> 00:13:44.221
She's the first girl who ever
really made me believe in love.


00:13:44.288 --> 00:13:48.392
Yeah, well, we all believe in
stupid things every now and then.


00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:51.929
Santa Claus, wrinkle cream,
zero-calorie Coke.


00:13:54.566 --> 00:13:58.202
Look, you're gonna
be fine, okay?


00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:01.822
Pain is temporary.
People get dumped every day.


00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:07.727
By the way, um--


00:14:09.063 --> 00:14:10.814
Love your outfit.


00:14:10.882 --> 00:14:14.151
Chartreuse is the perfect color
for your skin complexion.


00:14:14.219 --> 00:14:16.537
Thank you.


00:14:16.605 --> 00:14:18.772
Um, look,


00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:22.142
here's, uh--
here's my card.


00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:25.462
<i>And, uh, it was really nice</i>
<i>to meet you.</i>


00:14:50.589 --> 00:14:52.522
Stage-four crier?


00:14:52.591 --> 00:14:55.092
No, not at all. I--


00:14:55.159 --> 00:14:57.828
I've seen all sorts
of reactions from dumpees--


00:14:57.896 --> 00:15:02.432
fear, confusion,
throwing things, begging--


00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:05.268
but never anything
like this.


00:15:05.336 --> 00:15:08.405
He actually said
it was his fault.


00:15:10.742 --> 00:15:13.711
But he's a guy. Men never
admit to their own mistakes.


00:15:13.778 --> 00:15:17.881
I know. I mean, okay, let's say
hypothetically love does exist.


00:15:17.949 --> 00:15:21.819
Why kind of a girl would take
a guy like Rick for granted?


00:15:21.886 --> 00:15:26.741
Ugly nose. Fake boobs.


00:15:26.808 --> 00:15:28.743
Eating disorder.


00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:32.145
He needs to get
an eating disorder.


00:15:33.431 --> 00:15:35.365
Hey, Brit-Brit.


00:15:35.433 --> 00:15:38.118
Can you call
before you come?


00:15:38.185 --> 00:15:41.722
I don't have room on my speed dial.


00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:46.777
So, I forgot to tell Allan I'm leaving him
for Mike. You need to dump him for me.


00:15:46.845 --> 00:15:50.047
I'm supposed to meet him at
Aura in 20 minutes. Better hurry.


00:15:50.115 --> 00:15:51.998
Laters.


00:15:54.001 --> 00:15:57.404
Brit, we had
two more cancellations today.


00:15:57.472 --> 00:16:00.391
<i>They both say this other new
break-up service was cheaper.</i>


00:16:00.459 --> 00:16:02.859
Should we be worried?


00:16:02.927 --> 00:16:06.614
Also found this message
on your desk, Brit.


00:16:06.681 --> 00:16:08.794
TiVo <i>His Girl Friday
with Cary Grant--</i>


00:16:08.795 --> 00:16:09.483
<i>Uh-uh-uh.</i>


00:16:16.458 --> 00:16:21.294
Um, you two go take care of
Ashley's latest man-tard now.


00:16:21.362 --> 00:16:23.530
Go. Go, go, go, go!


00:16:30.037 --> 00:16:33.357
I, uh, just wanted
to thank you.


00:16:33.425 --> 00:16:35.893
Oh.
- I really appreciate what you do.


00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:40.164
If Sally and I had broken up face-to-face,
there would have been crying and screaming...


00:16:40.232 --> 00:16:44.201
and curling up in the fetal position,
and nobody needs to see that.


00:16:44.269 --> 00:16:47.504
It's no worries.
I'm a people person, so--


00:16:47.572 --> 00:16:50.423
Listen, I know this
is gonna sound forward,


00:16:50.491 --> 00:16:54.194
but, uh, I'm not a guy who
sits and mopes after a break-up.


00:16:54.262 --> 00:16:56.797
Would you join me
for dinner tonight?


00:16:58.499 --> 00:17:00.701
Uh--


00:17:00.768 --> 00:17:06.206
Oh, uh, company policy
outlaws dating dumpees.


00:17:08.509 --> 00:17:12.829
Wow. That so did not go
like I planned.


00:17:12.897 --> 00:17:16.033
Uh, I'm sorry.


00:17:16.101 --> 00:17:20.204
It's just, uh, you know,
when I saw you--


00:17:20.272 --> 00:17:22.273
Obviously,
you're beautiful.


00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:24.108
<i>And I guess I'm just</i>
<i>old school.</i>


00:17:24.175 --> 00:17:27.260
When I see someone I like,
I just charge full-speed ahead.


00:17:27.328 --> 00:17:31.531
It always seemed to work for my hero,
Cary Grant, and that's why I'm here.


00:17:34.035 --> 00:17:36.537
You okay?


00:17:41.526 --> 00:17:44.928
<i>Uh--</i>


00:17:46.982 --> 00:17:51.084
Damn, Gary.
Rough times.


00:17:51.152 --> 00:17:53.521
But Lindsay really
enjoyed her time with you.


00:17:53.588 --> 00:17:57.625
And, you know,
it's not you.


00:17:58.893 --> 00:18:00.894
No, actually, it is you.


00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:12.156
When Britney said you were
so ugly even Bill Clinton...


00:18:12.223 --> 00:18:15.125
wouldn't sleep with you,
she was just breaking the ice.


00:18:15.193 --> 00:18:20.147
She said, "Save your breath because you'll
need it to blow up your next girlfriend"?


00:18:20.214 --> 00:18:23.717
No. No, no, I am not laughing, sir.
It's just--


00:18:23.785 --> 00:18:25.920
Come on. It is funny.


00:18:25.987 --> 00:18:28.355
Hello? Hello, sir?


00:18:29.891 --> 00:18:32.042
What the hell, Brit?


00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:35.529
You're supposed to be a quick
and merciless ninja love assassin.


00:18:35.597 --> 00:18:38.398
Instead, you're Dr. Phil-ing
everyone's relationships.


00:18:38.466 --> 00:18:41.018
Relax. I'm on top of it.


00:18:41.085 --> 00:18:44.321
This other break-up service is
stealing our clients and, well,


00:18:44.389 --> 00:18:48.658
business is slower than
Tiffany taking the S.A.T.'s.


00:18:48.726 --> 00:18:51.728
Hey. Sometimes things
can be true <i>and</i> false.


00:18:51.796 --> 00:18:54.731
- Plus, these bills are just starting to--
- Hold that thought, okay?


00:18:54.799 --> 00:18:58.235
What? No, I'm sorry.
I'll be there in five.


00:18:58.303 --> 00:18:59.936
I'll see you guys tomorrow.


00:19:06.828 --> 00:19:11.131
I asked if I could use the bathroom an
hour ago. I'm still holding that thought.


00:19:11.199 --> 00:19:13.517
Go pee, sweetie.


00:19:21.792 --> 00:19:24.228
We even owe
the Arrowhead water guy.


00:19:24.295 --> 00:19:27.064
Ohh. Hi!


00:19:27.131 --> 00:19:30.401
Are you stuck in a bad relationship
that you want to get out of?


00:19:30.468 --> 00:19:34.671
Yes. For 27 years. But that's not
why I'm here.


00:19:34.739 --> 00:19:39.893
I'm Bob Green. I'm Britney's account
manager at Second Pacific Bank.


00:19:39.961 --> 00:19:43.170
I'm here regarding her
last few mortgage payments.


00:19:43.171 --> 00:19:44.114
What about them?


00:19:44.181 --> 00:19:47.384
She hasn't made any.


00:19:52.023 --> 00:19:56.259
Rick? Hello?


00:20:04.019 --> 00:20:07.003
I never believed in love
at first sight...


00:20:07.071 --> 00:20:08.788
until I saw you.


00:20:10.925 --> 00:20:16.230
You deserve that storybook movie
romance that you've always wanted,


00:20:16.297 --> 00:20:18.698
and I want to be
your leading man.


00:20:18.766 --> 00:20:23.921
I know I came on too strong,
but I can't help it.


00:20:23.989 --> 00:20:29.209
There's just something
about you, Britney Brooks.


00:20:29.276 --> 00:20:31.544
I wish I could quit you.


00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:35.833
No, don't quit me.


00:21:23.698 --> 00:21:27.233
Let's make
our own romantic movie.


00:21:43.735 --> 00:21:46.370
Wait. I think I have
onion breath.


00:21:46.438 --> 00:21:49.540
Frankly, my dear,
I don't give a damn.


00:22:25.827 --> 00:22:28.795
- Britney? Britney Brooks?
- Hmm?


00:22:28.863 --> 00:22:32.232
Sorry. Chuck Charleston.
I work with Rick.


00:22:32.300 --> 00:22:35.035
Oh.
- He has pictures of you everywhere...


00:22:35.103 --> 00:22:37.287
and I just totally recognized you.


00:22:37.354 --> 00:22:40.273
No way. I'm actually
meeting him here. Sit.


00:22:40.341 --> 00:22:42.693
Oh, thank you.


00:22:42.761 --> 00:22:48.381
Oh, Rick raves about you, about how
close you've become in such a short time.


00:22:48.449 --> 00:22:50.800
Yeah.


00:22:50.868 --> 00:22:52.969
And it scares him.


00:22:53.037 --> 00:22:56.273
That's why he feels it's best
to just nip it in the bud now.


00:22:56.340 --> 00:23:00.194
What? Uh-- I'm sorry.
- Yeah.


00:23:00.261 --> 00:23:04.565
Why, uh-- Why would he
tell you and not--


00:23:04.632 --> 00:23:06.567
Yeah.


00:23:06.634 --> 00:23:08.868
Yeah.


00:23:08.936 --> 00:23:11.588
Are you breaking up with me?


00:23:11.656 --> 00:23:14.841
Well, it's nothing personal.
It's what I do.


00:23:14.909 --> 00:23:18.297
Chuck Charleston,
break-up specialist. No?


00:23:18.298 --> 00:23:18.612
Okay.


00:23:18.613 --> 00:23:22.265
You used the "nip it
in the bud" speech?


00:23:22.333 --> 00:23:25.135
That's mine. I invented it.
It is copy--


00:23:25.202 --> 00:23:27.354
You are in a lot
of trouble, mister.


00:23:27.422 --> 00:23:29.973
Wait. Look, it's not him.
It's--


00:23:30.040 --> 00:23:33.376
No, wait. It's not him--


00:23:33.444 --> 00:23:35.128
Careful!


00:23:36.531 --> 00:23:39.416
That's pumpernickel!


00:23:39.484 --> 00:23:42.202
All right. Beat it, chuckles.


00:23:44.205 --> 00:23:46.473
Evidence. Evidence.


00:23:48.409 --> 00:23:52.545
Sorry about that, Brit.
Chuck's just a trainee in our business.


00:23:52.613 --> 00:23:54.297
<i>Our</i> business?


00:23:54.365 --> 00:23:57.017
Yeah.


00:24:00.070 --> 00:24:03.139
You're the other
break-up service?


00:24:04.358 --> 00:24:07.010
You pretended to like me?


00:24:07.078 --> 00:24:10.647
Whoa, whoa. I was just doing market research,
all right, checking out my competition.


00:24:10.715 --> 00:24:12.599
I couldn't know
that you'd fall for me.


00:24:12.667 --> 00:24:17.187
Besides, I was told you were this
emotionally tough businesswoman and, well,


00:24:17.255 --> 00:24:19.522
possibly not even into dudes.


00:24:19.590 --> 00:24:21.508
Anyway, Brooksy,
here's the deal.


00:24:21.576 --> 00:24:24.494
Love is the one thing in this
world that people will always need.


00:24:24.562 --> 00:24:28.231
E-Mate brings 'em together,
and E-Dump pulls them apart.


00:24:28.299 --> 00:24:31.835
I control both ends of love's production.
It's capitalism at its finest.


00:24:31.903 --> 00:24:34.454
You're Microsoft-ing
break-ups?


00:24:34.522 --> 00:24:36.723
Britney, I'm sorry.


00:24:36.791 --> 00:24:40.627
It's just business.
I never meant to hurt you.


00:24:40.694 --> 00:24:43.279
That's my line too,
you hack!


00:24:45.065 --> 00:24:47.767
Hmph.


00:24:47.835 --> 00:24:52.556
It's okay. You've been in this
situation before, just on the other side.


00:24:52.623 --> 00:24:57.344
Compose yourself and leave with dignity.
Hmm. Hmm.


00:25:09.306 --> 00:25:12.075
Loser.


00:25:15.747 --> 00:25:18.298
You know, for years
I told my dumpees...


00:25:18.366 --> 00:25:21.351
that life goes on
and it'll all be okay,


00:25:21.419 --> 00:25:24.254
but now I realize there aren't
plenty of other fish in the sea.


00:25:24.321 --> 00:25:26.423
Nope. All the good fish
have been caught.


00:25:26.491 --> 00:25:30.727
The ones left swimming have been
tossed back in by someone else.


00:25:30.795 --> 00:25:33.746
Come on.


00:25:43.658 --> 00:25:45.892
Oh, I love this song.


00:25:45.960 --> 00:25:48.161
Turn it off!
- Oh.


00:25:48.228 --> 00:25:52.431
God, I am so done with Rick.


00:25:52.499 --> 00:25:56.370
He's a lying, immature,
scummy, two-faced--


00:25:56.437 --> 00:25:59.389
Do you think, if I lost
10 pounds, he'd take me back?


00:26:01.709 --> 00:26:03.910
Oh.


00:26:03.978 --> 00:26:06.379
We need to tell her
about the mortgage.


00:26:06.446 --> 00:26:11.034
Not while she's in a serial stage.
It'll kill her.


00:26:12.886 --> 00:26:14.887
Air kisses all.


00:26:18.092 --> 00:26:22.328
You need to dump Mike for me.
Turns out he's not rich.


00:26:22.396 --> 00:26:26.099
He's got all these expensive-looking
paintings in his place,


00:26:26.167 --> 00:26:28.834
but he, like,
drew them himself.


00:26:28.902 --> 00:26:31.804
Ah, the nerve!


00:26:31.872 --> 00:26:37.310
Britney needs a break right now, Ash.
She's taking things one day at a time.


00:26:37.378 --> 00:26:40.113
No, no.


00:26:40.181 --> 00:26:44.784
If one more person tells me to
take things one day at a time, I'm--


00:26:44.852 --> 00:26:46.519
I'm gonna start taking things
two days at a time.


00:26:46.587 --> 00:26:49.923
Yeah. I'm gonna jump
from Monday to Thursday.


00:26:49.991 --> 00:26:52.893
If Rick wants a break-up
battle, he's gonna get one.


00:26:52.960 --> 00:26:55.762
You do not mess
with the master.


00:27:04.022 --> 00:27:06.790
Mmm.


00:27:06.858 --> 00:27:10.827
Britney, hey. It's really great to
see you. What are you doing here?


00:27:10.895 --> 00:27:12.779
Mike, Ashley is--


00:27:12.846 --> 00:27:17.183
Amazing. I know, I know.
She's like my own personal angel.


00:27:17.251 --> 00:27:20.953
Ashley, an angel?


00:27:21.021 --> 00:27:24.157
She may be the Antichrist.
I have priests looking into it.


00:27:24.225 --> 00:27:26.459
You have really
incredible eyes.


00:27:26.527 --> 00:27:30.914
<i>You and Ashley, you both have
these just amazing, piercing eyes.</i>


00:27:30.981 --> 00:27:32.916
<i>Every time she looks at me,</i>
<i>it's like, she's just--</i>


00:27:32.983 --> 00:27:37.254
you know, peeling back
the layers of my soul.


00:27:39.323 --> 00:27:41.091
Ashley's breaking up with you.


00:27:44.661 --> 00:27:46.596
What?


00:27:46.663 --> 00:27:49.099
Yeah, it's, uh--
it's what she does.


00:27:49.166 --> 00:27:53.019
I'm sorry, but it's over.


00:27:53.086 --> 00:27:55.888
Wait a minute.
Wait a--


00:27:55.956 --> 00:28:00.610
But I totally recommend the lobster
ravioli here. Get it with the Alfredo.


00:28:07.652 --> 00:28:11.888
I should've been nicer to her.
I should've treated her better.


00:28:11.956 --> 00:28:15.574
Been there--


00:28:15.642 --> 00:28:19.512
Do you think, if I gained
10 pounds, she'd take me back?


00:28:22.283 --> 00:28:25.951
Oh, no! Ashley!


00:28:26.019 --> 00:28:31.457
Steven, you're past due
for a dumping.


00:28:31.526 --> 00:28:35.128
They did?
Half the price?


00:28:36.497 --> 00:28:39.032
Okay. Bye.


00:28:39.099 --> 00:28:41.034
Rick's stupid company
is stealing...


00:28:41.101 --> 00:28:44.337
all our immature 20-something,
commitment-phobic males.


00:28:44.405 --> 00:28:47.741
I mean,
they're our meal ticket.


00:28:47.808 --> 00:28:50.109
Come on.
- Oh, Tiff.


00:28:50.177 --> 00:28:51.945
Come on.
- What are we gonna do?


00:28:52.013 --> 00:28:54.047
It's okay.
- We have to figure something out.


00:28:54.114 --> 00:28:55.999
We will.


00:29:02.106 --> 00:29:04.023
He was in no condition
to drive.


00:29:08.296 --> 00:29:10.497
Wait a second.


00:29:13.300 --> 00:29:18.121
You're Ashley's sister. You know
what kind of man she wants, right?


00:29:18.189 --> 00:29:19.806
Listen, I will--


00:29:19.874 --> 00:29:22.241
I will pay you anything you
want to help me win her back.


00:29:22.309 --> 00:29:26.613
Okay? Anything. I've got
maybe 10 grand in my savings.


00:29:26.680 --> 00:29:28.281
We'll take it!
- We'll take it!


00:29:28.348 --> 00:29:31.250
What?
- Yes.


00:29:31.318 --> 00:29:33.536
No, no. I don't get people
together, okay? I pull them apart.


00:29:33.604 --> 00:29:36.339
That'd be like Al Gore
selling S.U.V.s.


00:29:36.406 --> 00:29:38.258
Britney, but you don't understand.
Just help me, anything.


00:29:38.325 --> 00:29:40.593
Just tell me
what she's looking for.


00:29:40.661 --> 00:29:42.379
Money. Do you make a lot?


00:29:42.446 --> 00:29:45.648
I'm a Y.M.C.A. art teacher.


00:29:45.716 --> 00:29:48.451
Mm-hmm. Strike one.
Do you enjoy fine dining?


00:29:48.519 --> 00:29:50.353
I'm a vegan.


00:29:50.420 --> 00:29:54.557
Strike two. Ashley only enjoys
eating things that once had a soul.


00:29:54.624 --> 00:29:57.393
Do you like to travel?


00:29:57.461 --> 00:29:59.996
I've been to Bakersfield once.


00:30:00.064 --> 00:30:03.082
Strike three. Sorry, can't help you.


00:30:03.150 --> 00:30:05.702
Please. You don't understand. Listen,
Mike, you seem like a decent guy,


00:30:05.769 --> 00:30:09.739
and you're oddly attractive in a "George from
<i>Grey's Anatomy"</i> kind of way,


00:30:09.807 --> 00:30:14.794
but you have the one thing that Ashley
is just not interested in: heart.


00:30:14.862 --> 00:30:16.779
So--


00:30:27.541 --> 00:30:29.809
The Arrowhead guy too?


00:30:29.876 --> 00:30:33.613
Yeah. Your last few
mortgage payments bounced.


00:30:33.681 --> 00:30:37.934
We're gonna have to
pay them back fast, or--


00:30:38.002 --> 00:30:40.236
Or I lose everything.


00:30:42.106 --> 00:30:45.474
This is why love blows.
Why didn't you girls stop me?


00:30:45.542 --> 00:30:50.262
We'll fix it, Brit.
I'll work overtime.


00:30:50.330 --> 00:30:54.701
And I'll give back the stapler
I took from the supply room.


00:31:02.543 --> 00:31:06.680
Sorry, girls,
but you've been downsized.


00:31:13.120 --> 00:31:15.121
That's good.


00:31:23.997 --> 00:31:25.998
That's nice.


00:31:38.045 --> 00:31:41.815
Okay, guys, that's it.
See you Thursday.


00:31:44.084 --> 00:31:46.085
Good work.


00:31:55.062 --> 00:31:58.732
I knew it. I knew the power
of love would bring you back.


00:31:59.834 --> 00:32:04.371
Yeah, love.
Still 10 grand, right?


00:32:04.438 --> 00:32:06.439
Uh, yeah, sure.


00:32:06.507 --> 00:32:11.143
I mean, I'd pay anything to get
Ashley back. She was my muse.


00:32:14.147 --> 00:32:16.148
I'm sorry. Really.


00:32:18.586 --> 00:32:22.187
I painted this when I was with Ashley.
I couldn't stop painting.


00:32:22.255 --> 00:32:26.959
I had this artistic explosion in my
soul the entire week we were together.


00:32:27.027 --> 00:32:29.546
You got whipped in a week?
- And you know what?


00:32:29.613 --> 00:32:34.134
I even sold two of my pieces. I never
sold any of my art before I met Ashley.


00:32:34.201 --> 00:32:36.102
And now--


00:32:38.138 --> 00:32:42.408
all I can paint is this.


00:32:43.593 --> 00:32:47.664
Yeah. I need Ashley back,
Britney.


00:32:47.731 --> 00:32:51.333
I need my muse back. These kids are expecting
me to lead them in this mural contest.


00:32:51.401 --> 00:32:54.537
How am I supposed to lead them
when all I can paint is this?


00:32:57.041 --> 00:32:59.325
That's why I'm here.
So--


00:32:59.392 --> 00:33:03.797
What? You're gonna help--
- Yes.


00:33:05.365 --> 00:33:07.300
Oh! Yes!
- No.


00:33:07.367 --> 00:33:10.211
Thank you. Thank you.
Thank you. Thank you.


00:33:10.212 --> 00:33:10.470
Okay.


00:33:10.538 --> 00:33:12.171
Rule number one.
- Yes?


00:33:12.239 --> 00:33:15.542
Do not ever hug me again.


00:33:15.609 --> 00:33:17.610
Oh.
- Rule number two.


00:33:17.678 --> 00:33:21.681
Yeah?
- What I say goes. No questions.


00:33:21.749 --> 00:33:24.651
Really? Even if I have a--
Sorry.


00:33:24.718 --> 00:33:27.119
Rule number three:
no refunds.


00:33:30.607 --> 00:33:33.443
Within this building lies the
hottest collection of women...


00:33:33.511 --> 00:33:35.912
west of an MTV <i>Real World</i>
<i>casting call.</i>


00:33:35.979 --> 00:33:38.965
Hold your own in here
and there's hope for us yet.


00:33:39.032 --> 00:33:41.901
I'm allergic to dogs,


00:33:41.969 --> 00:33:45.170
but I have a cat.
- Great.


00:33:45.238 --> 00:33:50.760
See, women like that are similar to
Ashley in hotness and lack of humanity.


00:33:50.827 --> 00:33:54.064
So, consider this practice--
a flirting spring training.


00:33:54.131 --> 00:33:56.832
Britney, I don't want her.
I want Ashley.


00:33:56.900 --> 00:33:59.669
Yeah, and Ashley loves
confident men--


00:33:59.736 --> 00:34:02.705
men with the balls
to hit on anyone anywhere.


00:34:02.773 --> 00:34:05.675
God, how'd you meet
my sister in the first place?


00:34:05.742 --> 00:34:08.878
Oh, she, uh--
She sent me a text,


00:34:08.946 --> 00:34:11.381
said that I was hot,
to come over.


00:34:11.449 --> 00:34:13.616
Adorable.


00:34:13.684 --> 00:34:16.352
Well, if you can't handle hitting
on a girl you don't even care about,


00:34:16.420 --> 00:34:20.123
how do you expect to handle being
comfortable around a girl who you love,


00:34:20.191 --> 00:34:22.425
a girl who's your muse?


00:34:46.466 --> 00:34:49.419
Very nice. Maybe there
is hope for us yet.


00:34:49.486 --> 00:34:54.390
Well, that girl's married, but
I think she wants me to cat-sit.


00:34:54.458 --> 00:34:56.559
So, good?


00:34:56.627 --> 00:34:56.863
Huh?


00:34:56.864 --> 00:35:00.463
Ashley doesn't want a guy who
menstruates more than she does.


00:35:00.531 --> 00:35:04.467
Get back out there and prove to me
that you actually have a "Y" chromosome.


00:35:13.043 --> 00:35:15.244
Oh, uh, here.


00:35:15.312 --> 00:35:17.347
Let me get that. Yeah?


00:35:17.414 --> 00:35:20.316
Yes. Thank you so much.
- You're welcome.


00:35:20.384 --> 00:35:22.685
Say thank you, Leah.


00:35:22.753 --> 00:35:25.655
Uh, I'm Mike.
- Melanie.


00:35:25.723 --> 00:35:28.057
Nice to meet you.
- And you already met Leah.


00:35:28.124 --> 00:35:31.827
Give him a kiss. It's okay. It's okay.


00:35:34.180 --> 00:35:36.966
I'm so sorry. I'll get him.
Get back here.


00:35:37.034 --> 00:35:39.235
<i>Leah! Come back!</i>


00:35:40.987 --> 00:35:42.455
<i>Leah!</i>


00:35:43.657 --> 00:35:46.092
If people find out
where we're going--


00:35:46.159 --> 00:35:48.928
No, we're jobless, Tiff.
We need to save cash.


00:35:48.996 --> 00:35:53.232
This is a necessary evil.


00:35:53.300 --> 00:35:56.669
But-- But an outlet store?


00:35:56.737 --> 00:36:00.740
I'd be buying retail--
outdated retail.


00:36:00.808 --> 00:36:04.927
I wasn't looking at her chest.
I was trying to read her T-shirt.


00:36:04.995 --> 00:36:08.147
Something written on her ass too!


00:36:13.053 --> 00:36:15.604
Excuse me, ma'am,
but your boyfriend is--


00:36:15.672 --> 00:36:18.040
A big, fat jerk!


00:36:18.108 --> 00:36:21.945
Agreed. We can make that significant
other a lot less significant.


00:36:22.012 --> 00:36:25.314
Hi, Sarah. I'm Rick Barnes,
president of E-Dump.


00:36:25.382 --> 00:36:29.067
I represent Pat, and while he apologizes
for today's unfortunate incident,


00:36:29.135 --> 00:36:31.637
he feels that you've got
real trust issues.


00:36:31.705 --> 00:36:35.658
That's why he thinks it's best for
you two to go your separate ways.


00:36:35.726 --> 00:36:38.344
- Are you breaking up with me?
- Yeah.


00:36:38.412 --> 00:36:40.112
Yeah.


00:36:42.165 --> 00:36:47.237
Dude, check out my other site-- E-Mate.
A lot of potential rebound chicks.


00:36:47.304 --> 00:36:49.972
Ladies.


00:36:50.040 --> 00:36:51.991
Mm-mmm.


00:36:52.058 --> 00:36:56.061
Time to get our game faces on.


00:36:59.817 --> 00:37:02.318
Oh, sorry. Wrong game.


00:37:10.276 --> 00:37:12.712
<i>He'll dump you as soon</i>
<i>as the credits roll!</i>


00:37:22.990 --> 00:37:25.958
Oh, if it isn't the Matisse of mucus.
- Sorry, okay?


00:37:26.026 --> 00:37:30.029
I just didn't know you were gonna so quickly
throw me to the wolves-- Pomeranians.


00:37:30.097 --> 00:37:32.932
You and Ashley go together about
as well as socks and sandals.


00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:35.101
Okay? Let it go.


00:37:35.168 --> 00:37:39.305
Are you kidding me? No. I need
Ashley. I love her. Okay?


00:37:39.373 --> 00:37:42.458
Love is an illusion created by
the founders of Valentine's Day...


