with roses, all the time.


00:55:30.509 --> 00:55:32.611
Now every time I see them,
I think of him...


00:55:32.678 --> 00:55:35.947
and I remember
all the pain.


00:55:36.015 --> 00:55:37.949
Rick ruined red roses
for me.


00:55:39.919 --> 00:55:42.887
He also ruined bubble baths,
New York City...


00:55:42.955 --> 00:55:46.224
and most of my music collection,
including, sadly, my '90s Madonna.


00:55:49.061 --> 00:55:52.530
Ashley killed
frozen yogurt for me.


00:55:52.598 --> 00:55:55.000
Also, uh, hammocks,


00:55:55.067 --> 00:55:57.636
banana pancakes
and the color magenta.


00:55:57.703 --> 00:56:01.706
I lost French food, diet
cola and airplane flights to Rick.


00:56:01.774 --> 00:56:06.144
Da Vinci is dead to me. So are butterfly
kisses, Ping-Pong and reality TV.


00:56:06.211 --> 00:56:10.982
The beach, Pictionary, sweet tea,
iPods, slow dances, Cary Grant.


00:56:11.050 --> 00:56:14.318
Sunsets, sleeping in, strawberries
and John Denver's "Country Roads."


00:56:14.386 --> 00:56:16.755
Rick ruined
everything for me.


00:56:26.431 --> 00:56:28.499
Maybe I should
come back tomorrow.


00:56:44.917 --> 00:56:47.168
Have I really got you
in my arms again?


00:56:47.236 --> 00:56:49.537
Oh! Jack!


00:56:50.989 --> 00:56:55.393
Rick's company is huge,
and I'm just me.


00:56:55.461 --> 00:56:57.395
And now they have
my two best friends.


00:57:00.299 --> 00:57:04.486
Well, they're a heartless
corporation just in it for the money.


00:57:04.553 --> 00:57:06.821
You dumped people
out of love.


00:57:06.889 --> 00:57:09.324
Will you stop with that
awful four-letter word?


00:57:11.761 --> 00:57:15.831
You know, if the writers of these movies
you like so much never experienced love,


00:57:15.898 --> 00:57:18.667
they'd have no idea
how to portray it on screen,


00:57:18.734 --> 00:57:22.403
and you wouldn't have any idea
who Cary Grant is.


00:57:25.891 --> 00:57:28.727
You see, when a person has love
and they channel it into something,


00:57:28.794 --> 00:57:30.729
whether it's a painting...


00:57:30.796 --> 00:57:34.332
or a business that helps people
shed their unwanted exes,


00:57:34.399 --> 00:57:36.534
it becomes a force of nature.


00:57:36.602 --> 00:57:40.522
A passionate person fueled by love
is a force that no one can defeat.


00:58:14.740 --> 00:58:16.875
Just use that other color.


00:58:26.668 --> 00:58:29.637
All right. Can I grab
your brush for a second?


00:58:29.705 --> 00:58:31.489
Thank you.


00:58:31.556 --> 00:58:34.225
All right, guys, we're gonna do some
more passionate and stronger strokes.


00:58:34.292 --> 00:58:37.428
Just like this, all right?
And be vibrant with your colors.


00:58:37.496 --> 00:58:40.732
Because we are happy,
and this is a happy mural.


00:58:41.800 --> 00:58:44.869
Hi.
- Mmm.


00:58:44.937 --> 00:58:47.939
Uh, keep goin', guys.


00:59:11.930 --> 00:59:14.265
I went to that frat house
like you asked.


00:59:14.333 --> 00:59:17.635
I got at least five new names.
- Oh.


00:59:19.572 --> 00:59:23.140
And where would
our client list be?


00:59:24.777 --> 00:59:28.179
I mean, I should add the new names.


00:59:28.247 --> 00:59:30.515
Well, leave them
on my desk.


00:59:30.583 --> 00:59:34.218
No one sees the client list
but me and Rick. Hmm?


00:59:37.155 --> 00:59:39.290
<i>Oops.</i>


00:59:46.632 --> 00:59:49.501
Mmm! Thanks.


00:59:50.770 --> 00:59:54.439
No ways.


00:59:54.507 --> 00:59:57.609
Sorry. Oops.


00:59:57.676 --> 00:59:59.611
Right.


01:00:03.749 --> 01:00:05.500
What about her?


01:00:05.567 --> 01:00:08.603
Uh, purse doesn't match?


01:00:08.671 --> 01:00:11.172
No. You're not supposed to
wear white after Labor Day.


01:00:11.240 --> 01:00:15.443
Oh. Oh!
- And that's for ditching me last night.


01:00:15.511 --> 01:00:18.312
Well, I remembered how much you
appreciated our other night together.


01:00:18.380 --> 01:00:20.264
Yeah, but, last night,
I need--


01:00:21.450 --> 01:00:23.752
I mean, I wouldn't have
hurt you for staying.


01:00:23.819 --> 01:00:25.954
Okay, hang on. Stop.


01:00:26.022 --> 01:00:28.806
So, first, you're pissed
at me because I stayed.


01:00:28.873 --> 01:00:31.592
Now you're mad at me for leaving.
- Yeah.


01:00:31.660 --> 01:00:35.396
Well, how am I sup--
Oh, come on, Britney.


01:00:39.818 --> 01:00:42.670
Well, I'm sorry?


01:00:42.738 --> 01:00:45.940
Congratulations.
You passed.


01:00:46.008 --> 01:00:48.726
Passed what?
- The female-brain test.


01:00:48.793 --> 01:00:51.729
See, our logic is way more advanced
than your standard Earth male,


01:00:51.796 --> 01:00:55.233
yet we expect you to understand
even when we don't make sense.


01:00:55.300 --> 01:00:57.802
That makes no sense.
- Exactly.


01:00:57.869 --> 01:01:00.638
But you kept your cool
and followed the golden rule:


01:01:00.706 --> 01:01:03.408
"Always apologize to a girl
when she's upset."


01:01:03.475 --> 01:01:06.544
Especially when you didn't
do anything wrong.


01:01:06.612 --> 01:01:10.315
So, hang on.
All the crying last night--


01:01:10.382 --> 01:01:12.350
that was part
of this test?


01:01:12.418 --> 01:01:16.120
Yeah, of course.
I mean, come on. Me cry?


01:01:16.188 --> 01:01:19.156
Bah.
- Okay. 'Cause I was worried about you.


01:01:20.759 --> 01:01:23.461
That guy was progressively
lighter from head to toe.


01:01:23.529 --> 01:01:25.530
Who dresses him?


01:01:29.534 --> 01:01:32.553
Have you ever considered working
on the happy end of relationships?


01:01:32.621 --> 01:01:35.756
People don't need help falling in love.


01:01:35.824 --> 01:01:39.193
They have the Internet and
alcohol for that.


01:01:39.261 --> 01:01:42.964
But they do need someone to help
cushion the blow when it's over.


01:01:43.032 --> 01:01:45.300
'Cause no matter
how gently you dump someone,


01:01:45.367 --> 01:01:49.537
what your ex is really saying is,
"My life is better without you in it."


01:01:50.806 --> 01:01:54.208
Getting dumped is like
skinning your knee as a kid.


01:01:54.276 --> 01:01:57.611
I'm just the kiss from Mom
that makes it feel better.


01:01:57.679 --> 01:02:01.249
I really hope that one day you and
love get back on speaking terms.


01:02:01.317 --> 01:02:05.153
Love is just a leftover emotion
from our hairy ancestors.


01:02:05.221 --> 01:02:07.688
I mean, when your house is under
constant attack from woolly mammoths,


01:02:07.757 --> 01:02:10.091
then yeah, love and all that
other cutesy stuff are important.


01:02:10.159 --> 01:02:15.396
But today we have wireless everything.
We're self-sufficient.


01:02:15.464 --> 01:02:17.765
We don't need
to rely on each other.


01:02:20.669 --> 01:02:22.587
So, what about them?


01:02:22.654 --> 01:02:24.922
Probably been together
for over 30 years.


01:02:24.989 --> 01:02:26.841
Their youthful good looks
are gone.


01:02:26.908 --> 01:02:29.393
They've already gotten on
each other's every last nerve.


01:02:29.461 --> 01:02:32.680
And I'm sure they're not
in it for the sex anymore.


01:02:32.748 --> 01:02:35.382
So how do you explain the fact
that they're still together?


01:02:35.451 --> 01:02:37.452
How else
other than love?


01:02:40.422 --> 01:02:42.723
Senility and Viagra.


01:02:44.476 --> 01:02:48.112
I'm just saying.


01:02:48.179 --> 01:02:50.881
While I agree that her shirt
was cut sluttily,


01:02:50.949 --> 01:02:53.016
it also had a very humorous
slogan on the front,


01:02:53.084 --> 01:02:55.253
so clearly my client was looking
at that and not her boobs.


01:02:55.320 --> 01:02:57.488
So it's over. Deal with it.


01:02:58.523 --> 01:03:02.159
Well, pardon me.


01:03:02.227 --> 01:03:05.563
I don't know how I didn't see
this tall drink of handsome.


01:03:05.631 --> 01:03:08.666
Mm-mmm-mmm.


01:03:09.868 --> 01:03:13.003
Oh. Just as I thought.
Made in heaven.


01:03:15.607 --> 01:03:19.143
I'm on my way to Crunch
to do some pectoral flies.


01:03:19.210 --> 01:03:22.212
Mm-hmm?
- Care to spot me?


01:03:23.415 --> 01:03:25.349
Okay.


01:03:25.417 --> 01:03:29.353
Good work, Steven.
Your next dumping is on the house.


01:03:32.074 --> 01:03:34.108
Where's the client list?


01:03:39.014 --> 01:03:40.949
He's not talking.


01:03:41.016 --> 01:03:43.517
That's because
you gagged him, sweetie.


01:03:47.323 --> 01:03:50.124
Let me go!
