# We'd be together
till the end of time #


01:15:26.954 --> 01:15:29.890
# But time passed so quickly #


01:15:29.957 --> 01:15:32.292
# I guess
you changed your mind #


01:15:32.360 --> 01:15:34.528
# Though my head's a mess #


01:15:34.596 --> 01:15:37.597
# I've got nothin' left
without you #


01:15:37.665 --> 01:15:41.718
# And I hate how it feels #


01:15:41.786 --> 01:15:45.455
# I want to see you again #


01:15:45.607 --> 01:15:48.058
# How could this be the end #


01:15:48.125 --> 01:15:51.295
# Don't say good-bye #


01:15:51.362 --> 01:15:54.615
<i># Don't say good-bye #</i>


01:15:54.682 --> 01:15:57.234
# I know this time
it's for real #


01:15:57.301 --> 01:16:00.087
<i>Sorry, guys,</i>
<i>but you know what?</i>


01:16:00.154 --> 01:16:02.089
I know we're
better than this.


01:16:02.156 --> 01:16:04.357
And that's why
we're gonna start over.


01:16:04.425 --> 01:16:06.243
We're gonna put
our hearts into it,


01:16:06.310 --> 01:16:08.612
and we're gonna put
our souls into it.


01:16:08.680 --> 01:16:11.397
Yeah. Put some
sea-foam green into it.


01:16:11.465 --> 01:16:13.800
And remember, guys, we're
telling a story here.


01:16:13.868 --> 01:16:16.403
We're telling a story
about good versus evil,


01:16:16.471 --> 01:16:19.038
and we're telling a story
about love.


01:16:19.106 --> 01:16:21.425
What the hell, Mike?


01:16:21.492 --> 01:16:23.677
This is our D-day.
We're on a strict schedule.


01:16:23.744 --> 01:16:26.897
Ashley will be at Avalon by 10:15.
- Spider Club, 10:30.


01:16:28.299 --> 01:16:32.736
She asked me out.
- Ashley asked you out?


01:16:34.522 --> 01:16:37.791
Ashley never asks anyone out.
I mean, that's great.


01:16:37.859 --> 01:16:40.660
You got your muse back.
- I turned her down.


01:16:40.728 --> 01:16:43.363
What?


01:16:43.431 --> 01:16:45.916
I just thought that after the other ni--
- No, Mike, I need this!


01:16:45.983 --> 01:16:48.836
Okay? Or else
I lose everything.


01:17:22.303 --> 01:17:25.372
- Got your text.
- Yeah.


01:17:25.439 --> 01:17:27.641
You need something?


01:17:27.709 --> 01:17:30.344
I need my girls back.


01:17:33.280 --> 01:17:35.999
Bouquet, bouquet!


01:17:37.368 --> 01:17:39.302
Yea!


01:17:39.370 --> 01:17:41.788
I'm so sorry that I
downsized you girls.


01:17:41.789 --> 01:17:42.672
Mmm.


01:17:42.740 --> 01:17:45.225
- But I have a secret mission tonight.
- Ooh.


01:17:45.292 --> 01:17:46.501
You wanna get upsized?


01:17:46.502 --> 01:17:47.710
- Let's do it!
- Yes!


01:17:47.778 --> 01:17:48.945
Yes! Yes!


01:17:51.882 --> 01:17:55.018
Oh, I totally wanna
see you too, Rick.


01:17:55.085 --> 01:17:57.187
But, yeah, no, we're gonna
have to wait until tomorrow.


01:17:57.255 --> 01:18:01.057
I totally have plans with
someone else tonight. Laters.


01:18:10.835 --> 01:18:13.170
How did you know
I liked pink roses?


01:18:13.237 --> 01:18:16.639
Red ones got ruined.


01:18:21.495 --> 01:18:23.297
Keep feeding her wine, Mike.


01:18:23.364 --> 01:18:25.599
The higher her blood-alcohol level,
the better our chances.


01:18:37.544 --> 01:18:39.379
Okay.


01:18:47.188 --> 01:18:49.456
You're right, sir.
They're on the move.


01:19:00.534 --> 01:19:02.735
Oh. I've gotta go
powder my nosie.


01:19:02.804 --> 01:19:05.172
If the waitress comes,
I want--


01:19:05.239 --> 01:19:07.107
Merlot-- 73.5 degrees.


01:19:16.518 --> 01:19:19.335
Okay. Very nicely done.
We almost have balance.


01:19:19.403 --> 01:19:21.304
Go to the appetizer page.


01:19:23.257 --> 01:19:25.859
<i>Follow the script,</i>
<i>and we will be fine.</i>


01:19:27.361 --> 01:19:30.046
Okay. What if she does
something unexpected?


01:19:30.114 --> 01:19:31.832
Desserts. Here.


01:19:36.337 --> 01:19:38.121
Okay.


01:19:44.895 --> 01:19:48.698
Uh-- Okay, static.


01:19:48.766 --> 01:19:51.968
What's going on with the sound?
- Um, mike check, check. Can you hear me?


01:19:52.035 --> 01:19:54.271
You know what?
Forget about it. Don't even worry.


01:19:54.338 --> 01:19:56.439
You have taught me well.
I can do this on my own.


01:19:56.507 --> 01:19:59.688
No. We're screwed I
think it's the batteries.


01:19:59.689 --> 01:20:01.278
Here you go.


01:20:01.345 --> 01:20:03.246
Hi.
- Hi.


01:20:03.314 --> 01:20:05.966
Oh. Mm-mmm.
Okay.


01:20:06.033 --> 01:20:10.904
Match the diode up with its ionic
charge, or it won't circulate its power.


01:20:10.971 --> 01:20:14.241
Tiff?


01:20:14.308 --> 01:20:16.159
And he's wearing pink.


01:20:16.226 --> 01:20:19.579
- Shoot. She's coming! Battle stations.
- Go. Go.


01:20:26.403 --> 01:20:29.172
After dinner, you should
try the crème brûlée.


01:20:29.239 --> 01:20:31.240
It's Atkins-friendly here.


01:20:31.308 --> 01:20:33.343
The last time
we were together,


01:20:33.411 --> 01:20:37.046
you so gave off this
granola-loving, tree-hugging,


01:20:37.114 --> 01:20:39.882
"I give my salary
to the poor" vibe.


01:20:39.950 --> 01:20:43.486
I am so glad
I was wrong about you.


01:20:45.456 --> 01:20:49.642
Yeah, well, uh, you know,
I like to take things slow.


01:20:49.710 --> 01:20:53.714
When I meet someone, I prefer to
gradually reveal my personality as things--


01:20:53.781 --> 01:20:56.016
<i>Ashley!</i>


01:20:56.084 --> 01:20:57.868
You're being set up.


01:20:57.935 --> 01:21:02.160
This, uh, guy paid your sister
to help him get you back.


01:21:02.161 --> 01:21:02.456
What?


01:21:02.523 --> 01:21:04.474
Ashley, I understand your concern.
- Aw!


01:21:04.542 --> 01:21:06.726
Look!


01:21:08.412 --> 01:21:11.564
- Oh, crap.
- Pathetic.


01:21:11.632 --> 01:21:14.050
- What the hell's going on, Mike?
- Yeah, Mike.


01:21:19.941 --> 01:21:22.109
Brit-Brit?


01:21:23.961 --> 01:21:25.896
Ladies?


01:21:27.131 --> 01:21:30.366
How could you?
After everything I've done for you.


01:21:30.434 --> 01:21:34.187
She's just jealous, all right?
She's trying to break us apart.


01:21:34.255 --> 01:21:36.222
But I love you, Ashley.


01:21:40.544 --> 01:21:43.329
Ashes, no!
Remember Mike?


01:21:43.397 --> 01:21:47.934
He-He has fashion sense,
a limo and-- and those abs.


01:21:56.360 --> 01:21:59.529
Honey. It's really expensive.


01:21:59.597 --> 01:22:01.965
Hey! Back!
Give it to me! It's mine!


01:22:05.119 --> 01:22:08.855
So the ring is huge.
Come on, Mike. This is it.


01:22:08.922 --> 01:22:10.957
Don't quit on me.
Mike.


01:22:11.025 --> 01:22:13.460
I can't--
I can't do this anymore.


01:22:13.527 --> 01:22:16.562
Britney, all the games,
all the lies.


01:22:16.630 --> 01:22:20.283
I don't-- I don't even
think she's my muse anymore.


01:22:20.350 --> 01:22:22.735
What?


01:22:22.803 --> 01:22:25.789
Last night
when I kissed her,


01:22:25.857 --> 01:22:29.259
I-I didn't feel that spark
like before.


01:22:29.326 --> 01:22:32.095
It didn't feel as good
as when I kissed you.


01:22:33.814 --> 01:22:38.017
That wasn't a real kiss. It--
It was diversion. Doesn't count.


01:22:38.085 --> 01:22:40.070
Britney, the second
that we kissed,


01:22:40.137 --> 01:22:43.940
my mind exploded with thoughts and
feelings I didn't even know existed.


01:22:44.007 --> 01:22:46.376
My body tingled.
My lips were on fire.


01:22:46.444 --> 01:22:49.278
They were probably chapped.
I-- Here.


01:22:49.346 --> 01:22:52.699
Britney, you took charge of my life.
Okay?


01:22:52.767 --> 01:22:55.736
You... knew me.
You read me.


01:22:55.803 --> 01:22:59.506
No! No, I'm illiterate.
- You're incredible.


01:23:01.743 --> 01:23:03.744
You're incredible.


01:23:05.613 --> 01:23:07.781
I'm in love with you.


01:23:07.849 --> 01:23:09.115
No.


01:23:09.183 --> 01:23:11.334
No.


01:23:11.402 --> 01:23:15.338
Don't. Don't.
Don't do this.


01:23:15.406 --> 01:23:17.407
Just give it a chance.


01:23:22.413 --> 01:23:25.215
I can't date clients.


01:23:27.918 --> 01:23:30.620
You know what, Britney? If you want
to treat me like a client, fine.


01:23:30.688 --> 01:23:34.323
It's the logical choice, but I
know you felt something last night.


01:23:34.391 --> 01:23:36.443
You had to. Okay, listen.
- No. No.


01:23:36.510 --> 01:23:39.462
So for just once in your life,
think with your heart.


01:23:42.232 --> 01:23:45.969
Okay?


01:23:48.372 --> 01:23:52.375
I-- It's--
It's not you.


01:23:54.344 --> 01:23:56.345
It's me.


01:23:58.649 --> 01:24:01.084
I'm sorry.
I'm sorry.


01:24:08.375 --> 01:24:10.376
Cary Grant, Gregory Peck--


01:24:10.444 --> 01:24:13.429
those were real men,
men who don't exist today.


01:24:13.497 --> 01:24:18.201
- <i>Rule number one: Do not hug me.</i>
<i>- Get out!</i>


01:24:18.268 --> 01:24:21.154
- Is that all you got?
- What the hell, Mike?


01:24:21.221 --> 01:24:23.990
Considering your level of whippedness,
it's gonna take a lot more practice.


01:24:24.057 --> 01:24:26.493
And that's for ditching me
last night.


01:24:26.560 --> 01:24:28.462
Ow!


01:24:28.529 --> 01:24:34.434
# To guide you and lead you
through dark #


01:24:35.853 --> 01:24:39.406
# Into light #


01:24:48.165 --> 01:24:50.967
# Gotta know
what you're feelin' #


01:24:51.035 --> 01:24:53.737
# Wanna know
how you're dealin' #


01:24:53.804 --> 01:24:56.372
# With pain inside #


01:24:59.643 --> 01:25:02.495
# It's okay not to show it #


01:25:02.563 --> 01:25:05.398
# Takes some time
letting go #


01:25:05.466 --> 01:25:10.620
# All the hurt
you'll find #


01:25:10.687 --> 01:25:12.689
Robs?


01:25:16.210 --> 01:25:19.679
Perfect. That would be perfect, girl.


01:25:19.746 --> 01:25:21.664
I know what you're thinking.


01:25:21.816 --> 01:25:24.918
You're thinking,
"What was she thinking?


01:25:24.985 --> 01:25:28.855
"How could she pass up
the love of a great guy?


01:25:28.923 --> 01:25:32.558
A great guy with
a $10,000 check?"


01:25:32.626 --> 01:25:34.510
But I didn't earn
Mike's money.


01:25:34.578 --> 01:25:38.698
And I didn't
earn Mike either.


01:25:38.765 --> 01:25:40.850
He needs to be
with someone like him,


01:25:40.918 --> 01:25:43.636
someone--


01:25:43.704 --> 01:25:47.106
someone who still
believes in love.


01:25:47.174 --> 01:25:49.458
I just asked
if you had more boxes.


01:25:50.611 --> 01:25:52.546
Oh. Um--


01:25:53.497 --> 01:25:56.850
Nope. That's--
That's it.


01:25:56.918 --> 01:26:00.303
And you should've
kissed Mike.


01:26:00.371 --> 01:26:03.056
Shut up.


01:26:03.123 --> 01:26:06.659
Why do girls keep dumping
that cutie?


01:26:06.727 --> 01:26:08.728
Look at
the bright side, Brit.


01:26:08.795 --> 01:26:10.730
At least you kept him
away from Ashley.


01:26:10.797 --> 01:26:12.732
He would've never
been happy with her.


01:26:12.799 --> 01:26:17.203
Yeah. I mean, Mike's money might
help me keep all this stuff, but--


01:26:17.271 --> 01:26:20.740
At least I can still look
myself proudly in the mirror--


01:26:20.807 --> 01:26:23.243
if I had a mirror.


01:26:23.310 --> 01:26:26.246
Mmm. We'll do one
last check.


01:26:26.313 --> 01:26:28.248
Okay.
- Okay?


01:26:30.484 --> 01:26:32.485
It's gonna be okay.
- Okay.


01:26:33.720 --> 01:26:35.655
Come on.


01:26:47.050 --> 01:26:51.404
All right, come on in.
Let's get this over with.


01:26:51.472 --> 01:26:53.540
You know, people tell me
I had a mean job.


01:26:53.607 --> 01:26:56.376
You foreclose and rip people
out of their homes.


01:26:56.444 --> 01:26:59.245
Does that make you happy?


01:26:59.313 --> 01:27:01.430
<i>No.</i>


01:27:02.700 --> 01:27:04.634
Hi.


01:27:23.320 --> 01:27:26.639
I paid off the bank.


01:27:26.707 --> 01:27:29.876
What? Why?


01:27:31.311 --> 01:27:34.714
You paid me to help you get
back with Ashley, and I failed.


01:27:34.782 --> 01:27:37.450
I-- I didn't earn
your money.


01:27:37.518 --> 01:27:40.720
Oh, Britney. I hired you
to help me find my muse.


01:27:44.475 --> 01:27:46.743
I'm very happy
with your services.


01:28:00.891 --> 01:28:02.892
It's incredible.


01:28:06.278 --> 01:28:08.731
The kids and I worked on
it for three days straight.


01:28:08.799 --> 01:28:12.268
Just came together like all great
art does when you're inspired.


01:28:18.308 --> 01:28:21.110
He liked you.
He really did.


01:28:21.177 --> 01:28:25.047
You were great around the house,
amazing in the kitchen...


01:28:25.115 --> 01:28:28.317
and a generous,
yet gentle lover.


01:28:28.385 --> 01:28:30.820
But he just needs
to be with someone...


01:28:30.888 --> 01:28:33.022
a little less evil.


01:28:34.891 --> 01:28:39.612
Plus 1997 called and it wants its
unbuttoned Backstreet Boys shirt back.


01:28:41.782 --> 01:28:46.553
Unlike E-Dump, we offer a special
players' club card for macks like you...


01:28:46.620 --> 01:28:49.338
that offers discounts on all
"one-night stand" removals.


01:28:49.406 --> 01:28:52.541
When the clock strikes 4:00,
we'll get 'em out your door.


01:28:52.609 --> 01:28:54.727
Wait. Okay.


01:28:56.430 --> 01:28:59.031
Gary? Hi.


01:28:59.099 --> 01:29:01.818
I just felt like
we had a connection.


01:29:01.885 --> 01:29:03.953
Yeah, I miss you too.


01:29:04.021 --> 01:29:05.839
And now back to the financial news.


01:29:05.906 --> 01:29:08.307
Shares of E-Mate took an
Enron-esque nosedive today.


01:29:08.376 --> 01:29:11.378
The company's effort to break
into the break-up business bombed.


01:29:11.445 --> 01:29:13.780
Now that company
is getting dumped.


01:29:15.616 --> 01:29:18.084
I realized I have
a gift for starting relationships...


01:29:18.151 --> 01:29:20.086
as well as ending them.


01:29:20.153 --> 01:29:22.154
So I rebranded my company...


01:29:22.222 --> 01:29:25.958
and dedicated it to all aspects
of the most powerful force of all.


01:29:30.798 --> 01:29:34.217
Love Rocks. This is Britney.
How can I help you?


01:29:34.285 --> 01:29:36.219
Well, how can he
respect you, Steven?


01:29:36.287 --> 01:29:38.621
Stop putting out
on the first date.


01:29:41.225 --> 01:29:44.210
But I still enjoy going
back to my roots every now and then.


01:29:47.581 --> 01:29:49.632
Ah!


01:29:49.750 --> 01:29:52.252
Sorry to hear
about everything.


01:29:52.369 --> 01:29:55.171
Yeah, the break-up business--
it's a cruel one.


01:29:55.239 --> 01:29:58.307
This isn't over, Brooks.


01:29:58.375 --> 01:30:01.978
I'll be back, especially now
that I have Ashley.


01:30:02.046 --> 01:30:03.913
Yeah, about that.


01:30:03.980 --> 01:30:06.516
She doesn't really see this
relationship progressing.


01:30:06.583 --> 01:30:09.185
It's not her.
It's you.


01:30:10.954 --> 01:30:14.206
Seems there are lots
more people looking to fall into love...


01:30:14.274 --> 01:30:16.208
than fall out of it.


01:30:16.276 --> 01:30:18.277
Love blows.


01:30:20.630 --> 01:30:24.567
And that is the story
behind this painting.


01:30:24.634 --> 01:30:27.236
Thanks for choosing us, sir.
That money's going to good use.


01:30:27.303 --> 01:30:30.707
# Singin' na-na, na-na #


01:30:30.774 --> 01:30:32.942
# It's a beautiful life #


01:30:33.010 --> 01:30:35.945
And it's all
because of you.


01:30:36.013 --> 01:30:38.714
My muse.
# Na-na, na-na #


01:30:38.782 --> 01:30:41.717
# It's a beautiful life #


01:30:41.785 --> 01:30:44.586
# Yes, it is
Oh, oh #


01:30:44.654 --> 01:30:47.640
Hi. I'm Ashley.


01:30:47.708 --> 01:30:50.193
Okay, so maybe love
is a little more eternal...


01:30:50.260 --> 01:30:52.195
than I gave it credit for.


01:30:52.262 --> 01:30:55.181
Yep, I love love again.


01:30:55.248 --> 01:30:58.634
As some dead British guy once said that
it's "better to have loved and lost...


01:30:58.702 --> 01:31:01.103
than never to have
loved at all."


01:31:01.171 --> 01:31:04.974
Love is always in our hearts.
We can't lose it.


01:31:05.042 --> 01:31:07.944
But in case you did,
I can help.


01:31:08.011 --> 01:31:11.380
I'm Britney Brooks, the love consultant.
Give me a call.


01:31:11.448 --> 01:31:13.916
# What a beautiful life #


01:31:13.984 --> 01:31:16.251
# Yes, it is #


01:31:16.319 --> 01:31:18.688
# Na-na, na-na #


01:31:18.755 --> 01:31:20.856
# What a beautiful life #


01:31:23.093 --> 01:31:26.728
# Oh, na-na, na-na #


01:31:26.796 --> 01:31:29.698
# What a beautiful life #


01:31:29.766 --> 01:31:32.335
# Yes, it is #


01:31:32.402 --> 01:31:34.536
# Oh #


01:31:53.790 --> 01:31:57.126
# Still tryin' to
figure out what went wrong #


01:31:59.262 --> 01:32:03.599
# Thought we'd last forever
'cause we seemed so strong #


01:32:03.666 --> 01:32:07.236
# Singin' I love you #


01:32:07.304 --> 01:32:09.238
# Felt so right #


01:32:09.306 --> 01:32:13.842
# Now I lie awake
so many lonely nights #


01:32:15.778 --> 01:32:19.681
# Everyplace I go
and everything I see #


01:32:21.618 --> 01:32:25.754
# Reminds me of you
and how we used to be #


01:32:25.822 --> 01:32:31.193
# You took more than my heart
when you ran from me #


01:32:31.261 --> 01:32:36.732
# So please give me back
New York City #


01:32:36.799 --> 01:32:40.869
# You ruined airplane flights
and N.Y.C. #


01:32:40.937 --> 01:32:43.572
# Bubble baths
and some sweet tea #


01:32:43.640 --> 01:32:46.275
# I can't swim
I can't barbecue #


01:32:46.343 --> 01:32:49.178
# Green-eyed girls
now make me blue #


01:32:49.246 --> 01:32:53.416
# Butterfly kisses
fly away from me #


01:32:53.483 --> 01:32:55.951
# 'Cause I left my heart #


01:32:56.019 --> 01:32:58.721
<i># 'Cause I left my heart #</i>


01:32:58.788 --> 01:33:01.024
# 'Cause you broke my heart #


01:33:01.091 --> 01:33:05.194
<i># 'Cause you broke my heart #</i>


01:33:06.963 --> 01:33:12.334
# In New York City #


01:33:12.402 --> 01:33:16.772
# New York City #

